<title>GERMANY: VW silent on report of China problems.</title>
<headline>VW silent on report of China problems.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German car-maker Volkswagen refused to comment on a report, in Monday's edition of Der Spiegel news magazine, that its joint-venture with the Chinese car-maker First Automotive Works (FAW) faced possible closure.</p>
<p>In a copy of the report, obtained in advance by Reuters, Der Spiegel says that VW's factory in the northeast city of Changchun had moved deeply into the red and that production of its Jetta car had practically ceased.</p>
<p>Volkswagen said it had no comment to make on the report.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
